                "senderName": "NWS Melbourne FL",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued October 8 at 6:51PM EDT until October 8 at 8:45PM EDT by NWS Melbourne FL",
                "description": "FFWMLB\n\nThe National Weather Service in Melbourne has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nSoutheastern Brevard County in east central Florida...\n\n* Until 845 PM EDT.\n\n* At 651 PM EDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain across the warned\narea. Between 2 and 4 inches of rain have fallen. The expected\nrainfall rate is 1 to 2 inches in 1 hour. Additional rainfall\namounts of 1 to 2 inches are possible in the warned area. Flash\nflooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by heavy rain.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nMelbourne, Indialantic, West Melbourne, Melbourne Beach, Melbourne\nVillage, Melbourne Airport, Eau Gallie and June Park.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe especially cautious at night when it is harder to recognize the\ndangers of flooding.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.",
